---
source: disk/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"mount\")"
---
Mount a filesystem.

Four forms: - `mount` (no args) — list active mounts (like `findmnt`). - `mount -a` — mount every
entry from `/etc/fstab` not already mounted (skipping `noauto`, swap, and `ignore` entries). -
`mount <target>` — look up the target in `/etc/fstab` and mount it as configured. - `mount <source>
<target>` — direct mount. `<source>` may be a device path or a `LABEL=`/`UUID=` tag (resolved via
blkid).

Userspace-only and propagation features deferred to v1: `--move`,
`--make-{shared,slave,private,unbindable}`, `mount.<fstype>` helpers, loop devices, mtab/utab
writing, `-F/--fork`.

Usage: mount [OPTIONS] [SPEC] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [SPEC]
          Source (device, NFS export, tag, ...) — when only one positional is given, it's
          interpreted as the target instead

  [TARGET]
          Target mount point

Options:
  -a, --all
          Mount every entry from fstab. Skips entries with `noauto`, fstype `swap`, fstype `ignore`,
          or those whose target is already mounted. Filters via `-t` and `-O` apply

  -t, --types <TYPE>
          Filesystem type (e.g. ext4, tmpfs, proc). Required for direct mounts unless an option like
          `--bind` is given. With `-a`, limits which fstab entries to mount: a comma-separated allow
          list, or — if the first token starts with `no` — an exclude list (`-a -t nonfs,cifs` skips
          nfs and cifs)

  -O, --test-opts <LIST>
          With `-a`, limit to entries matching the comma-separated option test list. Each token must
          be present (`name`) or absent (`noname`); all conditions are ANDed

  -o, --options <LIST>
          Mount options (comma-separated). Combined with options from fstab when looking up a target

  -r, --read-only
          Mount read-only (alias for `-o ro`)

  -w, --rw
          Mount read-write (alias for `-o rw`, the default)

  -B, --bind
          Bind-mount (`MS_BIND`); two positional arguments are required

  -R, --rbind
          Recursive bind (`MS_BIND | MS_REC`)

      --remount
          Remount an already-mounted filesystem with new options

  -T, --fstab <FILE>
          Use `<file>` as the fstab instead of `/etc/fstab`

  -L, --label <LABEL>
          Source by label (alias for `<source>` = `LABEL=<label>`)

  -U, --uuid <UUID>
          Source by UUID (alias for `<source>` = `UUID=<uuid>`)

  -n, --no-mtab
          Don't write to /etc/mtab on success (no-op for us — we don't write mtab — but accepted for
          command-line compatibility)

  -v, --verbose
          Print what we're doing

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
